Given a list of ingredients, come up with a dish: Salt, Pepper, Onion, GarlicOne dish that could be made using Salt, Pepper, Onion, and Garlic as ingredients is roasted vegetables. Simply slice the onion and mince the garlic, then toss them with chopped vegetables of your choice (like potatoes, carrots, and bell peppers) in olive oil and season with salt and pepper to taste. Spread the mixture out in a roasting pan and bake at 425°F (220°C) for about 40 minutes or until the vegetables are tender and lightly caramelized. Serve as a delicious and healthy side dish.
