What is the formula for calculating the area of a triangle?The most common formula for calculating the area of a triangle is `Area = 1/2 * base * height`, where the base is the length of one of the sides of the triangle, and the height is the perpendicular distance from the base to the opposite corner of the triangle. Another way to calculate the area of a triangle is by using Heron’s formula, which requires knowing the length of all three sides. In this case, the formula for the area is `Area = square root of [s*(s-a)*(s-b)*(s-c)]` where `a`, `b`, and `c` are the lengths of the three sides, and s is the semi-perimeter of the triangle, calculated as `(a+b+c)/2`.
