Define what a neural network is.A neural network is a computational model that simulates the way the human brain processes information using interconnected nodes, referred to as neurons. A neural network is composed of layers of these neurons, where the first layer takes in inputs (like image pixels or sound frequencies), and the last layer produces desired outputs (like object classification or speech recognition). The outputs of one layer are fed to the inputs of the next layer, forming a connection between them. 

During training, the network learns by adjusting the weights of the connections between neurons to better predict the desired output based on the input. Once trained, neural networks can be used for tasks such as pattern recognition, prediction, classification, and decision making.

Neural networks have revolutionized the field of artificial intelligence and deep learning, and continue to drive advancements in technology.
