What is the scientific definition of metabolism?Metabolism refers to the entirety of all biochemical reactions that occur within an organism, including those reactions that break down molecules to generate energy (catabolism) and those that build up new molecules (anabolism). These reactions are facilitated by enzymes and are necessary for sustaining life through essential processes such as growth, reproduction, and response to the environment. Metabolism can also refer specifically to the breakdown of food and its transformation into energy.
Generate 3 marketing ideas to increase engagement on a product's social media account.1. Social Media Giveaway: Host regular giveaways for your product and incentivize the social media audience to participate by following the account, sharing the post, and tagging their friends in the comments. This would increase engagement, followers and potentially reach a new audience.

