In your own words, explain what a blockchain is.A blockchain is a distributed database or ledger that is managed by a network of computers, functioning as a decentralized and secure way to record and store information. It consists of a chain of blocks that hold batches of validated transactions or other information, which are linked together using cryptographic methods. Each block contains a record of multiple transactions and a reference to the previous block, forming an unchangeable and transparent chain of information. Its distributed nature, where the information is held across many computers and not controlled by a single entity, makes it resistant to manipulation and fraud, making it suitable for secure and transparent record keeping in various applications.
