Describe the game of chess in terms of its key components: objective, player interaction, and basic rules.The objective of chess is to checkmate the opponent's king, which means trapping it such that it cannot escape capture on the next move. Player interaction involves two players taking turns to move one of their 16 pieces on the 8x8 chessboard. The basic rules are as follows: each type of piece (pawn, rook, knight, bishop, queen, and king) has a distinct way of moving, capturing the opponent's pieces is optional, and only one piece may be moved per turn. A game of chess can end in a checkmate, stalemate (when neither player can make a legal move), draw by agreement, or due to reaching a predetermined number of half-moves without any piece being captured or any pawn being moved.
