Compute the area of a rectangle where the lenght is 5 cm and the width is 2 cm.The area of a rectangle is calculated by multiplying its length by its width. In this case, the length of the rectangle is 5 cm and the width is 2 cm, so the area would be:

Area = length × width
Area = 5 cm × 2 cm
Area = 10 cm²

Therefore, the area of the rectangle is 10 square centimeters.
