Create a Gantt chart showing tasks and their timelines.: Task: Create a website, Build a mobile app, Release a press statementUnfortunately, as a language model AI, I can understand and process text based tasks but I am not able to display graphic output, including charts. However, I can give you a text-based representation of a Gantt Chart. Here it is:

Here's an example of a text-based Gantt chart showing the tasks and their timelines:

| Task                  | Start Date | End Date   | Duration |
| --------------------- | ---------- | ---------- | -------- |
| Create a website      | 01/09/2022 | 02/08/2022 | 30 days  |
| Build a mobile app    | 02/09/2022 | 03/10/2022 | 30 days  |
| Release press statement | 03/11/2022 | 03/11/2022 | 1 day    |

This chart shows that the task of creating a website starts on 01/09/2022 and is scheduled to be completed on 02/08/2022, taking a total duration of 30 days. The next task, building a mobile app, starts on 02/09/2022 and is also scheduled to take 30 days, ending on 03/10/2022. Finally, the task of releasing a press statement is scheduled for 03/11/2022 and will take 1 day to complete. 

It's important to note that dates and duration are just an example, you can adjust the start and end date based on how long each task will realistically take.
Name three types of machine learning algorithms.Here are three main types of Machine Learning algorithms:
1. Supervised Learning: These algorithms use labeled training data to learn and make predictions on new data. This method includes algorithms such as linear regression, logistic regression, support vector machines, decision trees, and k-nearest neighbors.

2. Unsupervised Learning: These algorithms uncover hidden patterns and relationships within the data by clustering or dimensionality reduction. Examples of unsupervised learning algorithms are k-means clustering, hierarchical clustering, and principal component analysis.

3. Reinforcement Learning: These algorithms facilitate learning through the idea of "reward or punishment" based on the decisions that are made. The algorithm learns to associate particular decisions or behaviors with good or bad outcomes. An example of reinforcement learning is Q-Learning.
Determine the meaning of the word 'bemused'.The word "bemused" is an adjective that means puzzled or confused. It can refer to a state of being bewildered or disoriented, often associated with a lack of understanding or uncertainty. It is typically used to describe someone who is deep in thought, trying to make sense of something that they find perplexing.
