What is the logical fallacy of this argument?: If she really loved me, she would never make me angry.The logical fallacy in this argument is an example of a false dilemma or false dichotomy. False dilemma is a type of informal fallacy that involves presenting two options as the only two possibilities, when in reality, there may be others. In this case, the speaker is assuming that love and making someone angry are mutually exclusive, when in reality, it is possible to love someone and still unintentionally do something that makes them angry. This argument oversimplifies a complex human relationship and ignores other factors and complexities that may be at play.
