How many positive 3-digit numbers are divisible by 7?Note that 7 × 14 = 98 < 100 < 105 = 7 × 15 and 7 × 142 = 994 < 1000 < 1001 = 7 × 143. So the list of 3-digit numbers divisible by 7 is 105,112,…,994, and when we divide this list by 7, we get the list 15,16,17,…,141,142, which has 142 - 15 + 1 = 128 numbers.
