What are the roles of producers, consumers, and decomposers in a food chain?In a food chain, producers are organisms that create their own food through the process of photosynthesis, like plants. They are the base of the food chain, providing energy for other organisms. Consumers are organisms that eat other organisms to obtain energy. They are divided into primary, secondary, and tertiary consumers based on what they eat. Decomposers are organisms, such as bacteria and fungi, that break down dead or decaying organic matter into simpler substances. They return essential nutrients to the ecosystem, allowing the cycle to continue.
