Explain what rare earth elements are and list some examples.Rare earth elements, also known as rare earth metals, are a set of 17 chemical elements in the periodic table, specifically the 15 lanthanides along with scandium and yttrium. Despite their name, rare earth elements are relatively abundant, but they occur in low concentrations, and their extraction and processing can be difficult, costly and environmentally challenging.

Rare earth elements have unique chemical and physical properties that make them essential in a variety of high-tech and green technologies like electric vehicles, wind turbines, smartphones, and military equipment. 

Here is a list of some of the 17 rare earth elements:

1. Scandium (Sc)
2. Yttrium (Y) 
3. Lanthanum (La) 
4. Cerium (Ce) 
5. Praseodymium (Pr) 
6. Neodymium (Nd)
7. Promethium (Pm)
8. Europium (Eu) 
9. Gadolinium (Gd)
10. Terbium (Tb)
11. Dysprosium (Dy) 
12. Holmium (Ho)
13. Erbium (Er)
14. Thulium (Tm)
15. Ytterbium (Yb)
16. Lutetium (Lu)
17. Samarium (Sm)
Given the input, compose a poem.: A river flows gracefully through the town.A river flows gracefully through the town, 
Its waters, so pure, glistening and brown. 
