Explain what is meant by the phrase "digital divide".The "digital divide" refers to the gap between people who have access to modern information and communication technologies (ICT) such as the internet and computers, and those who do not. This divide can exist within a country or between countries, and it often reflects economic, geographic, or social inequalities. Those on the wrong side of the digital divide may miss out on important opportunities and services that others take for granted, such as online banking, telemedicine, remote work, or distance learning. Bridging the digital divide is seen as an important goal in ensuring that everyone can participate in and benefit from an increasingly digital world.
