Give a reason why is reading difficult for a certain personThere can be various reasons why reading might be difficult for a particular person. These reasons could be due to underlying conditions such as Dyslexia, which is a learning disability that affects reading fluency and comprehension, poor eyesight or hearing, Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder (ADHD) which affects focus and concentration, or a limited vocabulary and less exposure to the language being used in the reading material. Additionally, reading might be difficult if the content is too advanced or not interesting for the person or if the person has trouble processing and retaining information while reading. In some cases, inadequate education or lack of practice may also make reading a challenging task.
