Describe the role of an app developer in a company.An app developer in a company is responsible for designing, creating, and maintaining mobile and/or desktop applications. Their role includes writing clean and efficient code, collaborating with cross-functional teams, and actively participating in the software development life cycle. They work closely with designers and other developers to execute and achieve the company's vision for the app. They also test, debug, and resolve issues to ensure the app is user-friendly and meets the needs of the target audience. In addition, app developers are required to stay up-to-date with advancements in their field, ensuring that the app remains relevant and up to date with the latest technology and trends. Their role is critical to the success of the app and the company as a whole, as they bring ideas to life and provide valuable tools to users.
Create a program to check if the parenthesis of a string are balanced.Here is an example program written in Python to check if the parenthesis of a string are balanced:

```python
def is_balanced(string):
    stack = []
    for char in string:
        if char == '(':
            stack.append(char)
        elif char == ')':
            if not stack or stack.pop() != '(':
                return False
    return not stack

# Test cases

print(is_balanced('((()))'))  # True - balanced
print(is_balanced('()'))  # True - balanced
print(is_balanced('((())'))  # False - unbalanced
print(is_balanced('())'))  # False - unbalanced
```

In this program, we use a stack data structure to keep track of the opening parenthesis. If we encounter an opening parenthesis, we push it in the stack. If we encounter a closing parenthesis, we pop from the stack and check if it matches the opening parenthesis. In the end, if the stack is empty, then the parenthesis are balanced. Otherwise, it is unbalanced.
