Find the sum of the first 30 positive integers.The sum of the first 30 positive integers can be found using the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, which is:

sum = (n/2)(first + last)

Here, n is the number of terms in the series, so n = 30. The first term is 1 and the last term is 30. Plugging these values into the formula, gives:

sum = (30/2)(1 + 30)
sum = 15 x 31
sum = 465

Hence, the sum of the first 30 positive integers is 465.
