What type of government does Spain currently have?Spain is a parliamentary constitutional monarchy. This means that the monarch, currently King Felipe VI, is the head of state, while the Prime Minister, currently Pedro Sánchez, is the head of government. The powers of the monarch are largely ceremonial and symbolic, with the real executive power being vested in the Prime Minister and the Council of Ministers. The legislative branch of the government consists of the Cortes Generales, a bicameral parliament made up of the Congress of Deputies and the Senate.
