How many elements are found in the periodic table?As of January 2022, there are 118 known elements in the periodic table. These elements are organized by their atomic number, electron configurations, and chemical properties. Elements 1 through 118 have all been discovered or synthesized, with the most recent additions being nihonium (Nh), moscovium (Mc), tennessine (Ts), and oganesson (Og), which were added in 2016. It is important to note that the number of elements in the periodic table may increase in the future as new elements are discovered or synthesized.
