Given the following array: show all the possible subarrays: [1, 2, 3, 4]A subarray is a contiguous part of an array. An array of length n has n(n+1)/2 possible subarrays. For the given input [1, 2, 3, 4], we have the size of the array as 4. Thus, there are 4(4+1)/2 = 10 possible subarrays. The subarrays of [1, 2, 3, 4] are:

[1]
[2]
[3]
[4]
[1, 2]
[2, 3]
[3, 4]
[1, 2, 3]
[2, 3, 4]
[1, 2, 3, 4]
