Write a function in JavaScript that takes an array of numbers as input and finds the second highest number in the array.: [11, 2, 31, 7, 15]Here's the solution code in JavaScript:

```javascript
function findSecondHighest(arr){
  //remove duplicates from array
  let uniqueArray = [...new Set(arr)];
  
  //sort the array in descending order
  uniqueArray.sort(function(a, b) {
    return b - a;
  });

  // return second element
  return uniqueArray[1];
}

console.log(findSecondHighest([11, 2, 31, 7, 15]));
```
