Summarize the characteristics of a given type of animal.: GorillaA gorilla is a large and powerful primate that is native to Africa. They are known for their intelligence, strength, and social behaviors. Gorillas are typically divided into two species, the western and the eastern gorilla, with each further split into two subspecies. They have dark fur, with males developing silver hair on their backs when they reach maturity. Gorillas are herbivores and their diet consists mainly of plant material. They live in groups that are led by a dominant male, known as a silverback, who protects and directs the group. Gorillas are known for their displays of strength and aggression, but they are generally gentle and peaceful. They communicate through a variety of vocalizations, gestures, and body postures.
