Given a genetic mutation, explain what it means.: A deletion of the CFTR gene.A deletion of the CFTR gene means that certain portions of the DNA sequence of the CFTR gene have been removed or deleted. CFTR is an acronym for cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator, which is a protein responsible for the movement of salt and water in and out of cells. Since genes contain the instructions for building proteins, any change or mutation, including deletion, could alter the function of the protein it produces. In this particular case, a deletion in the CFTR gene could lead to the development of Cystic Fibrosis- a condition that affects the respiratory, digestive and reproductive systems and can lead to chronic lung infections and reduced ability to breathe over time.
