f (x) = x + 3 and g(x) = x^2 -6, what is the value of f (g(2))?Given f(x) = x + 3 and g(x) = x^2 -6, we are asked to find the value of f(g(2)). 

To get f(g(2)), we first need to find g(2): 

g(2) = 2^2 - 6 = -2 

Now we can find f(g(2)) by plugging in -2 for x in f(x): 

f(g(2)) = f(-2) = -2 + 3 = 1
