Come up with three interesting facts about the Mauna Kea volcano.1. Mauna Kea is the tallest mountain in the world when measured from its base on the ocean floor. Although it reaches an elevation of 13,796ft (4,205m) above sea level, its base extends about 19,700ft (6,000m) below the sea surface, making its total height from base to summit over 33,000ft (10,000m). 

2. Mauna Kea is considered to be a dormant volcano, with its last eruption occurring about 4,600 years ago. Its age is estimated to be around 1 million years old, making it one of the oldest of the five volcanoes that make up the Island of Hawaii. 

