3. Avoid using open fires and traditional stoves for cooking, heating, and lighting; instead, use cleaner fuels and cookstoves that reduce emissions.
4. Properly dispose of waste and avoid burning trash, which releases harmful pollutants into the air.
5. Choose to purchase and use products that are environmentally friendly and have a reduced impact on the environment.
