Create a program that generate a 100 to 500-word long text summarizing the content of the given text.: Between 1884 and 1885, German chemist August Kekulé developed the concept of the benzene ring: the idea that each of the six carbon atoms in benzene were connected to each other in a regular hexagonal arrangement with alternating single and double bonds.In the late 19th century, a German chemist named August Kekulé made a pioneering advancement in the field of chemistry by introducing the idea of the benzene ring. This concept, which emerged between 1884 and 1885, proposed that the six carbon atoms in benzene were arranged in a hexagonal pattern, with bonds alternating between single and double connections. Kekulé's theory laid an essential foundation for the understanding of aromatic compounds and became a crucial piece of knowledge for chemists.
