Calculate the area of an equilateral triangle with side length 15 cm.The formula for calculating the area of an equilateral triangle is `A = (sqrt(3) / 4) * a^2`, where `a` is the length of a side of the triangle. 

In this case, the length of each side of the equilateral triangle is `15 cm`, so we can plug this value into the formula to get:

A = (sqrt(3) / 4) * (15^2) 
A ≈ 97.43 cm²

So, the area of an equilateral triangle with side length 15 cm is approximately 97.43 cm².
