Find a specific example of the given keyword.: Keyword: Humanitarian effortsOne specific example of humanitarian efforts is the disaster response to the 2010 Haiti earthquake. The earthquake, which struck Haiti on January 12, 2010, caused widespread devastation and loss of life. In response, a massive and coordinated international relief effort was launched.

Governments, international organizations, and non-governmental organizations (NGOs) from around the world provided aid in the form of funding, medical assistance, food, water, and shelter. For example, the United Nations launched an appeal for $562 million to provide immediate assistance to the people of Haiti and the World Food Program (WFP) ramped up its existing programs to feed millions of people in the country.

Volunteers from NGOs such as Doctors Without Borders, the Red Cross, and Save the Children, among others, provided medical care, distributed relief supplies, and helped to rebuild homes and infrastructure. Many individuals and private organizations also donated money and resources to support the relief effort.

These humanitarian efforts helped to save lives and provide essential support to those affected by the earthquake, demonstrating the power of collective action to make a difference in times of crisis.
Create a connection between the two given concepts.: Concept 1: Evolution
Concept 2: AdaptationEvolution and adaptation are closely related concepts in the study of biology. Evolution refers to the change in the genetic makeup of a population over time, while adaptation refers to the process by which an organism becomes better suited to its environment, thereby increasing its chances of survival and reproduction. These two concepts are interconnected in that adaptation is one of the mechanisms that drive evolution. As a population of organisms adapts to its environment over time, its genetic makeup changes and, ultimately, the population evolves. Through this process of natural selection, species are able to adapt and evolve to better survive in their environment.
