If sqrt(5 + x) + sqrt(20 - x) = 7, what is the value of (5 + x)(20 - x)?We first square both sides of the equation sqrt(5 + x) + sqrt(20 - x) = 7 to obtain (5+x)+2sqrt(5+x)sqrt(20-x)+(20-x)=49. 

Next, we simplify this equation to get to 2sqrt((5+x)(20-x))=24. 

Finally, we solve for (5+x)(20-x)=(24/2)^2=144.
Write a function which reverses the words in a sentence, but not the order of the words.```
def reverse_words(sentence):
    words = sentence.split(" ")
    for i in range(len(words)):
        words[i] = words[i][::-1]
    return " ".join(words)
```
