Write an alternative historical outcome to the Boston Tea Party if the British had been able to catch the Americans involved in the event, and describe the implications this would have on the Revolutionary War.In the alternative historical outcome, the British authorities successfully apprehended the American colonists who were involved in the Boston Tea Party. As a result of their capture, tensions between the American colonies and Great Britain skyrocketed, as the British imposed even stricter control in response to the defiant act. More punitive legislation would follow, and traditional political negotiation methods that might have given the colonies some autonomy would be abandoned. The Revolutionary War would likely have commenced sooner, the uprising would become more widespread, and the determination of the colonies to achieve independence would have been strengthened. The ultimate outcome of the war might have remained the same, with the American colonies gaining independence from Britain, but the cost in terms of lives lost and the duration of the conflict could have increased significantly.
