Predict the end result of the following reaction:: CHCl3 + OH- →The reaction between CHCl3 (chloroform) and OH- (hydroxide ion) will result in the formation of HCO- (formate ion) and Cl-, with the release of two molecules of HCl (hydrochloric acid) as a byproduct. The net ionic equation for this reaction is written as:

CHCl3 + 3OH- → HCOO- + 3Cl- + 2H2O.

The formation of formate ion is typically achieved through the dehydrohalogenation process, where three hydrogen atoms from the chloroform molecule are sequentially replaced by three hydroxide ions, ultimately resulting in the formation of formate ion.
