Calculate the surface area of a sphere with radius 5The formula to calculate the surface area of a sphere is given by A = 4πr^2, where "A" is the surface area and "r" is the radius of the sphere. 

Plugging in the value of r = 5 into the formula, we get: 

A= 4 x π x 5^2
  = 4 x π x 25
  = 100π

So, the surface area of a sphere with radius 5 is 100π square units.
Generate a correct C++ program for the following logic.: Given a positive number N, print the numbers from 1 to N in reverse order.```c++
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;
int main()
{
    int N;
    cout << "Enter a positive number N: ";
    cin >> N;
    for (int i = N; i >= 1 ; --i) // loop from N to 1 in reverse order
    {
        cout << i << " ";
    }
    return 0;
}
```
