Find the hypotenuse of the right triangle.: Side A = 8 cm, Side B = 6 cmThe hypotenuse of a right triangle can be calculated using the Pythagorean theorem, which states that in a right triangle, the square of the length of the hypotenuse is equal to the sum of the squares of the other two sides. 

In this case, side A is 8 cm and side B is 6 cm, so we can use the Pythagorean theorem to find the length of the hypotenuse:

Hypotenuse² = Side A² + Side B²
Hypotenuse² = 8² + 6²
Hypotenuse² = 64 + 36
Hypotenuse² = 100

Taking the square root of both sides of the equation, we find that the hypotenuse of the right triangle is 10 cm.
Describe the look and feel of an ideal website.An ideal website would have an aesthetically pleasing design that encompasses a coherent color scheme, high-quality images and graphics, and easy-to-read fonts. The layout would be simple, intuitive, and uncluttered, making it easy to navigate and find the information the user is seeking. The content would be well-organized, concise, and presented in a way that is engaging and easy to understand. White space would be used effectively to break up blocks of text and create a feeling of openness and breathing room, while a logical hierarchy would make it easy to follow the flow of information. Overall, the look and feel of an ideal website would be one that is visually appealing, user-friendly, and provides a seamless and enjoyable browsing experience.
