Convert the percentage to a fraction.: 65%65% can be converted to a fraction by dividing 65 by 100. This gives us a fraction of 65/100. We can further simplify this fraction by dividing both the numerator (top number) and the denominator (bottom number) by the greatest common factor (GCF). The GCF of 65 and 100 is 5, so we can simplify to (65/5)/(100/5) = 13/20. Hence, the fraction representation for 65% is 13/20.
