List four measures to prevent the spread of COVID-19.1. Wear a mask: Wearing a mask can help to prevent respiratory droplets from being expelled into the air and onto surfaces, reducing the spread of the virus. 

2. Practice social distancing: Maintaining a distance of at least six feet from others, especially in crowded or enclosed spaces, can help to reduce the risk of transmission. 

3. Wash your hands frequently: Regular handwashing with soap and water for a minimum of 20 seconds can help to remove any virus that may be on your hands, preventing infection. 

4. Avoid touching your face: Refraining from touching your face, particularly your mouth, nose, and eyes, can help to reduce the risk of infection, as these are the primary entry points for the virus.
Write insertion sort in Java.: [7, 1, 3, 5, 9]Here's an implementation of insertion sort in Java:

```
public static void insertionSort(int[] arr) {
    for (int i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {
        int key = arr[i];
        int j = i - 1;
        while (j >= 0 && arr[j] > key) {
            arr[j + 1] = arr[j];
            j = j - 1;
        }
        arr[j + 1] = key;
    }
}
```

To use this method to sort the array `[7, 1, 3, 5, 9]`, you would call it like this:

```
int[] arr = {7, 1, 3, 5, 9};
insertionSort(arr);
System.out.println(Arrays.toString(arr));
```

This would output the sorted array: `[1, 3, 5, 7, 9]`.
Evaluate the following expression: 6 - (4 + 1)The expression 6 - (4 + 1) can be evaluated in two steps. First, solve the expression inside the parenthesis, which is 4 + 1 = 5. Then substitute this value back into the expression to get 6 - 5 = 1. The final result is 1.
