The lines y=5x+3, y=-2x-25 and y=3x+k intersect at the same point. What is the value of k?To find the value of k, we can start by finding where the lines y=5x+3 and y=-2x-25 intersect. Setting them equal to each other gives us the equation 5x+3 = -2x - 25, which can be solved for x to give x = -4. To find y, we can plug x back into either equation, giving y = 5*(-4) + 3 = -17.

Now that we have the point of intersection, we can plug in its x and y values into y=3x+k to solve for k. Plugging in -4 and -17 for x and y gives us -17 = -12 + k, which we can solve for k to get k = -5.
