Summarize the article  'Discovering the Science Behind Manta Ray Flying'The article 'Discovering the Science Behind Manta Ray Flying' discusses the fascinating way in which manta rays move through the water. These large fish are able to "fly" through the water using their large, wing-like pectoral fins, which they flap in a way that is similar to the motion of a bird's wings. Scientists are studying the mechanics of manta ray swimming to better understand this unique mode of locomotion, and to see if the principles could be applied to underwater vehicles. The article also talks about the importance of preserving manta ray populations, which are threatened by overfishing and habitat loss.
