Input two sets and determine if they are disjoint or not.: A = {3, 5, 7} 
B = {4, 6, 8}In order to determine if two sets are disjoint, we need to check if they have any elements in common. If the two sets have no elements in common, then they are disjoint.

In this case, set A has the elements {3, 5, 7} and set B has the elements {4, 6, 8}. It is clear that none of the elements from set A are present in set B and vice versa.

Therefore, sets A and B are disjoint.
