Given two tables, combine the tables and generate a view.: Table A:  student

Name   | Age  | Grade
------------------
John   | 20   | A

Table B: score

Name   | Test_1| Test_2
------------------------
John   | 50    | 80Based on the input, we can combine the two tables, Table A (student), and Table B (score) using the SQL JOIN clause. The resulting view, Table C, will include information from both tables:

Table C: student_score

Name   | Age  | Grade | Test_1 | Test_2
---------------------------------------
John   | 20   | A     | 50     | 80

A SQL statement that can be used to generate the above view is:

```
SELECT 
     A.Name,
     A.Age,
     A.Grade,
     B.Test_1,
     B.Test_2
FROM 
     student A
INNER JOIN 
     score B
ON  
     A.Name = B.Name
```
