Think step by step: How would you prepare a vegetarian pasta dish using tomatoes, onions, garlic, olive oil, and Parmesan cheese?1. Gather ingredients: tomatoes, onions, garlic, olive oil, Parmesan cheese, pasta (e.g., spaghetti or penne), and salt and pepper for seasoning.\n2. Prepare vegetables: dice onions, mince garlic, and chop tomatoes, keeping them separate.\n3. Heat a large pan over medium heat, add olive oil, and then add the diced onions. Cook until onions become translucent.\n4. Add minced garlic to the pan, and cook for a minute, stirring constantly to avoid burning the garlic.\n5. Add chopped tomatoes to the pan, cook for a few minutes while stirring occasionally, allowing the tomatoes to release their juices and soften.\n6. Taste and season the sauce with salt and pepper as needed.\n7. Simultaneously, bring a large pot of salted water to a boil and cook pasta according to package directions until al dente.\n8. Drain pasta and add it to the pan with the tomato sauce, tossing well to coat the pasta evenly.\n9. Serve immediately, topped with grated Parmesan cheese.
