What is the meaning of the phrase "never judge a book by its cover"?The phrase "never judge a book by its cover" is a metaphorical expression that cautions against making judgments or evaluations about someone or something based solely on outward appearance or superficial characteristics. It means that one should not make assumptions about the worth, value or character of a person or thing simply based on their appearance or what is immediately visible. Instead, one should take the time to get to know the person or thing in question, and base judgments on more substantial evidence. The phrase is often used to encourage people to look beyond first impressions and strive for a deeper understanding of others.
