Calculate the fraction of a circle that a given angle subtends.: Angle = 60°If the angle subtended is 60 degrees, then the fraction of the circle that the angle subtends is equal to the ratio of the angle to the total angle of the circle, which is always 360 degrees. This can be calculated as follows:

Fraction of circle = Angle / Total angle of circle
Fraction of circle = 60 degrees / 360 degrees
Fraction of circle = 1/6

Hence, an angle of 60 degrees subtends 1/6 of a circle.
