Write the conclusions of the article given below.: This study examined the effects of educational interventions on reducing teenage substance use. The study found that teens who received the intervention were significantly less likely to use cigarettes, marijuana, and alcohol. However, there were no significant differences in other drugs. There was also no difference between males and females or in different socio-economic statuses.In conclusion, the study showed that educational interventions were effective in decreasing cigarette, marijuana, and alcohol use among teenagers. However, the interventions did not have a significant impact on the use of other drugs. There were also no differences in the effectiveness of the interventions based on gender or socio-economic status. Overall, the findings suggest that educational interventions aimed at preventing substance use can play an important role in reducing certain types of substance use among teenagers.
