Describe the relationship between the nouns and pronouns in the sentence: "She invited Joe and he to dinner."In the sentence "She invited Joe and he to dinner," the pronoun "she" refers to the subject of the sentence, the person who is doing the action of inviting. "Joe" is a proper noun that is the direct object of the verb "invited," indicating the person being invited to dinner. The pronoun "he" is used in place of a noun and is also the direct object of the verb "invited" indicating another person being invited to dinner. The relationship between the pronouns and nouns in this sentence is that they are used to identify the subject and direct objects in the sentence, indicating who is doing the action and who is being affected by the action.
