Develop a multiple-choice question related to a fundamental concept in physics, ensuring the question has one correct answer and at least three plausible incorrect answers.Which of the following best explains why a book resting on a table does not accelerate downward even though it is under the influence of gravity?

(A) The book is stationary, so there is no force acting upon it.
(B) The normal force from the table exerts an equal and opposite force to gravity, resulting in a net force of zero.
(C) The book is in a state of equilibrium, meaning gravity does not affect it.
(D) The gravitational force and the centrifugal force cancel each other out.

Correct answer: (B) The normal force from the table exerts an equal and opposite force to gravity, resulting in a net force of zero.
