Identify and explain the rhetorical device used in the sentence.: This storm will not be a light breeze, it will be a tornado of change.The rhetorical device used in the sentence is a metaphor. A metaphor is a figure of speech in which a word or phrase is applied to an object or action to which it is not literally applicable. In this sentence, the storm is being compared to a tornado, representing a powerful and significant change. By describing the storm as a tornado, the metaphor conveys the intensity and the impact of the change that will occur.
