Identify the 3 goals of user-centered design and explain each briefly.1. Effectiveness: Ensuring that users can achieve their goals and complete tasks using the interface. This is critical for guaranteeing that users find value when interacting with a system or product.\n2. Efficiency: Allowing users to complete tasks quickly and with minimal effort. This is important for both maximizing user satisfaction and minimizing frustration or excessive cognitive workload.\n3. Satisfaction: Providing a pleasant and enjoyable user experience, which not only covers the aesthetics of the interface but also overall usability and learnability. A satisfying experience promotes user engagement, loyalty, and positive word-of-mouth.
