Read the following report on a recent soccer match and give a brief summary, focusing on key events and the final result.: Last night, the home team Arsenal faced off against Liverpool in a highly anticipated match. Arsenal started aggressively from the very beginning, dominating possession early in the game. However, in the 27th minute, Liverpool's star striker, Mohamed Salah, scored a stunning goal from 25 yards out, making the score 1-0. In response, Arsenal continued to press but were unable to pierce Liverpool's defense. As the first half came to an end, the score remained 1-0 in favor of Liverpool. In the second half, Arsenal returned with renewed energy and finally equalized in the 63rd minute when their midfielder, Granit Xhaka, scored off a set piece. With both teams tied at 1-1, the game became highly competitive, with each team fighting for the lead. However, neither team could produce a winning goal by the end of regulation time. As the final whistle blew, the match ended in a 1-1 draw.In a hotly contested match between Arsenal and Liverpool, both teams fought hard, but ultimately finished with a 1-1 draw. Liverpool's Mohamed Salah scored a remarkable long-range goal in the 27th minute to give them the lead. Arsenal eventually equalized in the 63rd minute, thanks to a well-taken set piece by Granit Xhaka. Despite a spirited battle by both teams, neither managed to score a winning goal before the final whistle.
