Write a description of the biggest galaxy in the universe.The galaxy IC 1101 is currently known as the largest galaxy in the observable universe. It is located about 1 billion light years away from Earth in the constellation of Serpens. This elliptical galaxy spans approximately 6 million light years in diameter, which is much larger compared to our Milky Way galaxy, that has a diameter of around 100,000 light years. IC 1101 is truly a giant, with an estimated stellar mass of about 100 trillion stars. It is believed that this massive galaxy was formed through the collision and merging of several smaller galaxies, making it a prime example of the concept of galactic cannibalism. The galaxy is so large that it extends beyond its home cluster and its stars, gas and dust reach into the intergalactic medium. It is also an active galaxy, meaning that it has an active galactic nucleus that emits a large amount of energy, due to the presence of a supermassive black hole at its center.
Write a poem about joy.Joy is in the smallest things
The sight of a sunset’s wings
The song of a bird on a breeze
The laughter of children at ease

Joy hides in the budding blooms
Like secrets revealed in their tombs
The silence of a peaceful night
That looms beneath the stars so bright

Joy is found in the dawn of day
When the sun comes out to play
In the sparkle of the summer rain
That washes away every pain

This is joy, meant to be embraced
For it can fill any empty space
Let it fill you up inside
And cast away your tear-soaked pride.
