This chapter from the 2014 Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change (IPCC) report discusses the impacts of climate change on human health. The authors discuss the increased risk of heat stress, air pollution, and the spread of infectious diseases. They also explore the potential co-benefits of climate change mitigation efforts, such as an improvement in air quality, which could result in significant health benefits. This chapter is a valuable source of information on the current state of knowledge on the health impacts of climate change.

4. Kinney, P. L. (2018). Interactions of Climate Change, Air Pollution, and Human Health. Current Environmental Health Reports, 5(1), 179-186.

