What are the APA style guideline?.APA style guidelines refer to the formatting and citation style used in academic writing to ensure uniformity and consistency. The guidelines cover various aspects of writing, including formatting, citing sources, and referencing. Some of the key guidelines include using double-spaced text, including a title page with author details and paper title, using a 12-point font, including in-text citations and references. Additionally, the APA style emphasizes the use of past tense and active voice, avoiding biased language and using figures and tables to support research findings.
