Identify the pattern in the following series: 1, 4, 7, 11, ?The pattern in this series is that each number is obtained by adding an increasing number to the previous number. The first number, 1, is obtained by adding 0 to it, so the next number 4, is obtained by adding 3 to the previous number (1 + 3 = 4). The next number, 7, is obtained by adding the same amount, 3, to the previous number (4 + 3 = 7). Then, the following number, 11, is obtained by adding a larger amount, 4, to the previous number (7 + 4 = 11). So, following this pattern, the next number in the series would be obtained by adding 5 to 11, resulting in 16. Thus, the next number in the series is 16.
