How many nonnegative solutions are there to the equation x^2 = -4x?The equation x^2 = -4x has only one nonnegative solution. We can rearrange the equation to x^2 + 4x = 0, then factor it as x(x+4)=0. The solutions are x=0 and x=-4, and only x=0 is nonnegative.
