Describe the process of artificial selection and provide an example.Artificial selection, also known as selective breeding, is a process in which humans deliberately choose specific traits to be passed on to the next generation of organisms. This technique has been extensively utilized in agriculture, horticulture, and animal husbandry to produce advantageous characteristics and increase the diversity of plants and animals. The process involves selecting individuals with desirable traits and breeding them, ensuring these traits become more prominent in future generations while eliminating unfavorable ones. A classic example of artificial selection is the domestication of wild plants and animals, such as developing maize from the wild grass teosinte. This was achieved by farmers selectively breeding plants with larger, more nutritious kernels over thousands of years, eventually transforming this wild grass into the maize we recognize today.
Come up with a list of five questions that can be used to interview a political candidate.Here are five potential questions that could be used to interview a political candidate: 

1. What motivated you to enter politics and pursue a role in public service? 
