3. How do you intend to reach across the political divide and work with members of different parties or factions to achieve your goals? 
4. Can you discuss a time when you faced a difficult decision and talk us through the process you used to make that choice? 
5. What measures do you support to promote transparency and accountability in government?
Pretend you are a professional photographer. Explain the importance of the rule of thirds in photography.As a professional photographer, I can tell you that the rule of thirds is an essential technique in creating visually compelling and balanced images. The rule of thirds involves dividing an image into a 3x3 grid, with two equally spaced horizontal lines and two equally spaced vertical lines. By aligning the subject or key elements of an image along these lines, or at their intersections, this technique helps to draw the viewer's attention to the most important parts of the image. Additionally, applying the rule of thirds can create a sense of depth and movement, making the image more engaging and dynamic. Many photographers use this technique because it is widely acknowledged to improve the overall aesthetic quality and visual interest of a photograph.
Describe the visual effect of a single beam of light entering a dark room.When a single beam of light enters a dark room, it can create a striking visual effect known as a "light shaft" or "ray of light". The beam appears as a linear column of light stretching from the source, such as a window or an opening, to the surface it illuminates. Depending on the conditions, such as the presence of dust or water droplets in the air, the beam itself may be visible as it travels through the room due to the light scattering off the particles. Within the beam, objects and surfaces are brightly illuminated, while the surrounding areas remain in relative darkness. This contrast can create a dramatic and atmospheric scene, with the beam of light providing a focal point in the room. Overall, the visual effect of a single beam of light entering a dark room is one of stark contrast and drama, highlighting the power of light to transform a space.
