Suppose there is a (fictitious) country named Lando with population of 9 million people and GDP of 1 trillion USD. From this information, calculate the GDP per capita.GDP per capita is the total GDP of a country divided by its population. In this case, Lando has a GDP of 1 trillion USD and a population of 9 million people. So, the GDP per capita can be calculated as follows:

GDP per capita = GDP / Population 
               = 1 trillion USD / 9 million people 
               = 1,000,000,000,000 USD / 9,000,000 people
               ≈ 111,111.11 USD

So, the GDP per capita of Lando is approximately 111,111.11 USD.
