Explain what a "root cause analysis" is.A root cause analysis is a systematic approach used to identify the underlying reasons for an incident or a problem. It involves breaking down an issue into its fundamental components, examining the sequence of events that led to the problem, and determining why it occurred in the first place. The goal of root cause analysis is to determine the underlying causes of a problem so that measures can be taken to prevent it from happening again in the future. This type of analysis is commonly used in industries such as manufacturing, healthcare, and engineering as a way to improve processes, increase efficiency, and reduce risks.
