Design a mascot for a virtual assistant.Our virtual assistant mascot would be an adorable, friendly, and approachable robot named "Vira". Vira has big, round eyes that give her a curious and empathetic look, and her body is in the shape of a teardrop, giving her a unique and memorable silhouette. She has a bright and welcoming smile that puts people at ease, and her arms extend out in a welcoming gesture, reinforcing her helpful nature.

Vira is small in size and can fit in the palm of your hand, making her easy to carry around wherever you go. She is made from a soft and durable material that is pleasant to the touch, and she comes in a variety of vibrant colors, including blue, pink, green, and yellow.

Vira is not just cute – she is also smart and capable. As a virtual assistant, she can help you with a wide range of tasks, from sending reminders to organizing your schedule and answering questions. She is always eager to learn and improve, which means that the longer you work with her, the more helpful she becomes.

Overall, Vira is the perfect mascot for a virtual assistant – friendly, approachable, and always ready to help.
Find the probability that a two digit number is divisible by 3.The probability that a two digit number is divisible by 3 is 30/90.

Explanation: 
A two-digit number can be any number from 10 to 99, which gives us a total number of possible outcomes as 90. All the numbers divisible by 3 from this list are 12, 15, 18, 21, … 96, 99, which makes the total of 30. Hence the probability of choosing a two digit number which is divisible by 3 is 30/90 which simplifies to 1/3 or about 0.33.
Suggest two alternatives for conserving energy.1. One effective way to conserve energy is by practicing energy-efficient habits at home and in the workplace. This can involve simple changes like turning off lights and electronics when not in use, adjusting the thermostat to a more moderate temperature, using energy-saving light bulbs, and unplugging chargers when they are not in use.

2. Another alternative for conserving energy is by investing in renewable energy sources, such as solar, wind or hydroelectric power. These sources are sustainable and do not produce harmful emissions like traditional fossil fuels. More and more people are installing solar panels on their homes or businesses to harness the power of the sun to generate electricity, reducing their reliance on non-renewable energy and lowering their energy bills in the process.
